    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Marcus's Food Waste Webpage\r\n\r\nMarcus wants to make a webpage about reducing food waste but doesn't know how to write HTML or CSS. Instead, they've provided you with a description and a potential screenshot:\r\n\r\n> \"I want to make a webpage about reducing food waste because I think it's something everyone should care about. I want each tip to look like its own little box on the page, with soft rounded edges. The writing inside should be bold so it feels like it matters.\"\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/6b82d497dd9963953ddb05db5d07b1fb-image-1774473981136.png\" style=\"width: 30%\" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1) Use AI tutor to help build this page. Ask it to make changes to this page step-by-step.\r\n    - Be specific about the elements, sizes, borders, and which elements they apply to\r\n2) Keep prompting until the webpage it's \"close enough\" to their vision!\r\n    - It doesn't have to perfectly match the image, but try to get it close to the style and layout!\r\n\r\nOnce you've compared your result to Marcus's vision: press the Continue button!\r\n\r\n**Hint:** This puzzle involves `<section>` and `<p>` tags in HTML, and the `border-radius` and `font-weight` properties in CSS.",
