        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "contents": "Reducing Food Waste\n\nPlan Your Meals\nBefore you go grocery shopping, plan out what you'll eat for the week. This helps you buy only what you need and avoid letting food go bad in the fridge.\n\nStore Food Properly\nLearn how to store different types of food correctly. Some fruits and vegetables last longer outside the fridge, while others need to stay cold.\n\nUse Your Leftovers\nGet creative with leftovers instead of throwing them away. Last night's roasted vegetables can become today's soup or wrap filling.\n\nCompost What's Left\nIf food does go bad, composting is a much better option than the trash. Compost breaks down into nutrients that can help a garden grow.",
          "active": true,
          "folderId": "0"
        }
      },
